# Copy this file to .env and fill in values as needed.
# The pipeline runs with NO keys at all (defaults to the free, keyless
# Pollinations.ai image provider, falling back to a local mock generator
# if there's no network). The variables below are only needed if you want
# to switch providers.

# Which image generation provider to use: pollinations | ideogram
# ("mock" also works on the CLI for a fully offline run.)
IMAGE_PROVIDER=pollinations

# Which Pollinations model to ask for. Left unset the endpoint picks its
# own, which in practice returns 768x768 no matter how large a size is
# requested -- so bigger output sizes get upscaled from that and look
# soft. Some models honour larger dimensions; try one here and check the
# size the results page reports.
POLLINATIONS_MODEL=

# Ideogram -- the higher-quality option, and the one aimed at graphic
# design rather than photography: it holds typography, posters and
# brand-style layouts together where a general model smears them. 1536px
# long edge. Create a key under API Keys at https://developer.ideogram.ai
#
# Billing note: the API is funded separately from an ideogram.ai
# subscription. Plan credits are spent by the web app and buy nothing
# here, so an account showing plenty of them still returns 402 until a
# payment method and a prepaid balance are added on the API dashboard.
IDEOGRAM_API_KEY=
# A model slug -- ideogram-v3 (default) or ideogram-v4 (latest). It goes
# straight into the request URL, so putting anything else here (an API
# key, say) produces a 404 rather than an obvious error.
IDEOGRAM_MODEL=ideogram-v3

# DeepL -- who translates the copy when "Copy language" is not English.
# Optional: with no key the app uses Google's free, unauthenticated
# endpoint instead, which works right up until it doesn't. That endpoint
# counts about five requests a second and 200,000 a day against whoever
# shares your IP, tells you neither number, and answers an exhausted
# quota with an HTML error page rather than an error -- so a campaign
# comes out in English hours later with no obvious cause.
#
# A free DeepL key is 500,000 characters a month and ends in ":fx"; the
# app reads that suffix to pick api-free.deepl.com over api.deepl.com,
# because sending a free key to the paid host answers 403 and looks for
# all the world like a bad key. Sign up at https://www.deepl.com/pro-api
#
# With a key set, DeepL translates and the free endpoint stays as the
# fallback -- for the languages DeepL lacks (Hindi, for one) and for a
# month that runs out. You can also paste the key into the box at the top
# of the web form instead of editing this file.
DEEPL_API_KEY=
